[h2][b]New features:[/b][/h2]

[list]
[*] New Roguelike mechanic in "Eternal Suffering" mode, adding an EXP system when killing monsters;
[*] 72 skill cards added in "Eternal Suffering" with various effects and rarity levels;
[*] Stage 3 added;
[*] First boss available in stage 3: "Devermon";
[*] Added visual lighting effects in the new stage;
[*] New moving platforms;
[*] New Alice letter in stage 3;
[*] "Flappydenptio" minigame added to the game;
[*] 5 cutscenes added to the game (expected 11 in the final version);
[*] EXP gained from each enemy in "Eternal Suffering" can vary based on factors such as shooting accuracy, time of death, number of Eclipses, among other variables;
[*] Enemies become more damaging, faster, and have more life based on the number of Eclipses the player survives in Eternal Suffering;
[*] During the Eclipse, various enemies are summoned (with the number increasing with each Eclipse);
[*] Control scheme selection (Windows, Xbox, Playstation and Nintendo);
[*] The control scheme changes the buttons displayed during the tutorial and menu screens;
[*] Buttons appear in the menu when using a gamepad and disappear when using keyboard and mouse;
[*] 3 Stars added for completing all stages (1 for completing the stage, 1 for eliminating all enemies in the stage, and 1 for collecting all letters in the stage);
[*] Full Gamepad support added;
[*] Added unique projectile impact effects for each weapon color;
[*] Option to enable or disable controller vibration;
[*] Devermon added to the Bestiary;
[*] EXP and Score display during "Eternal Suffering" gameplay;
[*] Level, Eclipses, Score, Enemies killed, Time, and Accuracy display during "Eternal Suffering" pause screen;
[*] Active enemies in the stage display during "Campaign" mode gameplay;
[*] Time, Enemies killed, Secrets (Alice letters), Deaths, and Accuracy display during "Campaign" mode pause screen;
[*] Control scheme selection option added in the Control settings menu;
[*] Game menus completely redesigned in a new style;
[*] Alice's letter diary added with the Bestiary;
[/list]

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44382118/f049154d8f661370c6fbecaee385dd51b5502d28.png[/img]

[h2][b]Corrections:[/b][/h2]

[list]
[*] Visual effects of weapon impact explosions modified;
[*] All Alice letters have been rewritten;
[*] Lava modified (transparency effect removed, and lighting effect modified);
[*] Life and damage of some enemies have been changed;
[*] Overall game graphic quality improvements, choosing between High, Normal, or Low quality;
[*] Enemy bodies stop following the game view in Low quality to improve performance;
[*] Modification in how the Sword slash is launched;
[*] Modification in how enemies appear in "Eternal Suffering";
[*] Texture errors fixed in all stages;
[*] Shadowing errors fixed in all stages;
[*] It is possible to navigate menu buttons with the gamepad using both the analog stick and the D-Pad;
[*] Menu navigation improvements using the Gamepad;
[*] Some enemy activation locations in the campaign have been corrected;
[*] Weapon selection wheel with gamepad support;
[*] Achievements "Bestiary," "Dear Alice," and "Ruthless" with progression numbers;
[*] Tutorial texts modified;
[*] Removed the "Color Correction" option from video settings and replaced it with "Scenery Effect" (which modifies some screen effects in specific stages);
[*] Bestiary removed from the pause menu, accessible only through the designated button;
[*] Adaptive music and sound effects during the menu;
[*] Fixed texture error when changing from high quality to normal quality;
[*] Different music during the reading of letters and the bestiary;
[*] Positioning and visibility of some active enemies in the scene modified;
[*] Time between flower spawns in "Eternal Suffering" modified;
[*] Map border modification;
[*] Alice's letters no longer appear after collecting them and completing the level;
[*] Dust effects on level 1 doors fixed;
[/list]

